TRICIÓN EN PATOLOGÍA DEL TUBO DIGESTIVO:This section discusses nutritional management in digestive tract pathologies, particularly focusing on pancreatitis.", "ABSTENCIÓN ENÓLICA:Abstención enólica refers to the cessation of alcohol consumption, which is crucial for managing pancreatitis and preventing further complications.", "TUBO DIGESTIVO:The \"TUBO DIGESTIVO,\" or digestive tract, is a vital anatomical structure responsible for processing food and facilitating digestion and nutrient absorption. It serves as the pathway through which enteral nutrition is administered directly to patients, highlighting its importance in clinical settings. The functionality of the tubo digestivo is crucial for determining the type of nutritional support required, especially in medical conditions such as pancreatitis, where specific nutritional management is necessary. Additionally, the tubo digestivo can be the subject of various diagnostic explorations to assess its health and functionality. Overall, the tubo digestivo plays a central role in both the digestive process and the management of nutritional needs in patients.", "DOLORES:", "AMERICAN COLLEGE OF GASTROENTEROLOGY:The American College of Gastroenterology is a professional organization that provides guidelines for the management of gastrointestinal diseases, including acute pancreatitis.", "CRITICAL CARE MEDICINE:Critical Care Medicine is a specialized field within medicine that focuses on the diagnosis and management of life-threatening conditions. This specialty encompasses a wide range of severe medical issues, including critical cases such as pancreatitis. Practitioners in Critical Care Medicine often utilize advanced techniques and tools, such as central venous catheters, to provide optimal care for critically ill patients. \n\nIn addition to clinical practice, Critical Care Medicine is also represented in academic literature through a peer-reviewed journal that publishes research findings related to critical care and intensive care medicine. Furthermore, the Society of Critical Care Medicine plays a vital role in this field by providing guidelines and recommendations for the management of critically ill patients, which includes specific protocols for treating patients with burn injuries. Overall, Critical Care Medicine is essential for addressing complex medical emergencies and improving patient outcomes in critical situations.", "RAN B:Ran B is an author who collaborated on research regarding early severe acute pancreatitis.", "BERGER HG:Berger HG is an author involved in the study of early severe acute pancreatitis.", "MITCHELL RM:Mitchell RM is an author who has written about pancreatitis in the Lancet.", "BYRNE MF:Byrne MF is an author who has contributed to the literature on pancreatitis.", "BAILLIE J:Baillie J is an author who has published work on pancreatitis.", "TENNER S:Tenner S is an author who has provided guidelines for the management of acute pancreatitis.", "DEWITT J:DeWitt J is an author who has contributed to the guidelines on acute pancreatitis.", "VEGE SS:Vege SS is an author associated with the American College of Gastroenterology guidelines on acute pancreatitis."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}